BrailleBridge — Bill of Materials (BOM)

1. Overview

This document lists the proposed electronic and mechanical components required to develop BrailleBridge, a modular, repairable, low-cost refreshable Braille display.

The initial prototype will focus on one six-dot Braille cell. The proposed architecture allows future expansion to four cells (24 dots), subject to successful validation of the initial prototype.

Component prices and final quantities will be confirmed during procurement.

2. Electronic Components

No.	Component	Specification	Quantity for Initial Prototype	Purpose
1	Arduino Uno R3	ATmega328P-based development board	1	Processes text input and controls the system
