4. Proposed Expansion to Four Cells

The longer-term target is a four-cell display containing 24 Braille dots.

Component	Proposed Quantity for Four Cells
Arduino Uno R3	1, subject to controller-capacity validation
PCA9685 servo driver boards	2
MG90S micro servos	24, plus 6 spare servos as proposed in the project plan
Braille pins	24
Pin guides	4 cell assemblies, subject to final mechanical design
Power supply	To be validated against the final system’s measured current requirements
Supporting mechanical parts	To be determined from the final CAD assembly

The four-cell configuration is a stretch goal and will be considered only after the six-dot prototype has been validated.

5. Electrical and Integration Considerations

* The Arduino Uno R3 will communicate with the PCA9685 boards over I²C.
* The proposed PCA9685 I²C addresses are 0x40 and 0x41.
* The Arduino Uno R3 uses A4 for SDA and A5 for SCL.
* The initial six-dot cell is intended to use channels 0–5 on the first PCA9685 board.
* Servo power requirements must be considered separately from the Arduino’s logic-power requirements.
* The power supply rating, wiring, connectors and grounding arrangement must be checked against the actual components before operation.
* Servo positions and mechanical travel limits must be calibrated to avoid pin jamming or excessive force.
* Output-enable control and the startup sequence will be validated during integration.

